<title>HONG KONG: HKFE, NYMEX to begin trading link on June 13.</title>
<headline>HKFE, NYMEX to begin trading link on June 13.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong Futures Exchange (HKEF) said on Monday it and New York Mercantile Exchange (NYMEX) would begin an electronic trading link on June 13 at 4 a.m. Hong Kong time (2000 GMT, June 12).</p>
<p>The link, agreed upon in September 1996, will provide HKFE members direct access to NYMEX products, including crude oil, gold, silver, copper, heating oil, gasoline, natural gas, propane, and electricity, during the hours that they are electronically traded, the HKFE said in a statement.</p>
<p>NYMEX ACCESS electronic trading terminals have been installed in Hong Kong in preparation for the link, it said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
